---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import WidgetWrapper from '~/components/ui/WidgetWrapper.astro';
import Headline from '~/components/ui/Headline.astro';
import FAQs from '~/components/widgets/FAQs.astro';
import CTABanner from '~/components/widgets/CTABanner.astro';
import SectionBg from '~/components/ui/SectionBg.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Is It Time to Replace Your Roof on Oahu? | R&C Roofing',
  description:
    'Wondering if your roof is at the end of its life? Learn the signs that may point to roof replacement, when repair may still make sense, and how R&C evaluates aging roofs on Oahu.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>

  <!-- P-01 Hero — white -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="py-8 md:py-12 max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-[42px] md:text-[56px] font-medium leading-[115%] tracking-tighter font-heading mb-6">
        Is My Roof at the End of Its Life?
      </h1>
      <p class="block text-[20px] md:text-[24px] font-medium font-heading text-heading mb-6 leading-[130%] tracking-tight">
        An Older Roof Does Not Automatically Need to Be Replaced
      </p>
      <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-4 mb-8">
        <p>Maybe your roof has started leaking more often. Repairs are becoming more frequent. Roofing material looks worn, damaged, or different from how it used to look.</p>
        <p>Or maybe nothing dramatic has happened. You simply know the roof has been there a long time and want to know how much longer you can reasonably rely on it.</p>
        <p>Age matters, but age alone does not determine whether you need a new roof. R&C Roofing Contractors evaluates aging roofs within its Oahu service area to determine whether continued repair still makes sense or whether replacement should be considered.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Have R&C Evaluate Your Roof</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-secondary">Find Out What Condition Your Roof Is In</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium text-muted">(808) 888-2524 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Hawaii Contractor License C-33642</p>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <SectionBg variant="white" />
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Signs it is time for a closer look — grey -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <Headline title="Is Your Roof Telling You It Is Time for a Closer Look?" classes={{ container: 'mb-4 md:mb-6' }} />
    <p class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8 md:mb-10">
      No single symptom automatically means a roof has reached the end of its useful life. The pattern of problems matters.
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 shadow-card">
      <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse bg-white dark:bg-slate-900">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-accent/20 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700">
            <th class="px-5 py-4 text-[13px] md:text-[14px] font-semibold font-heading text-heading uppercase tracking-wide w-1/2">What You Are Seeing</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-4 text-[13px] md:text-[14px] font-semibold font-heading text-heading uppercase tracking-wide w-1/2">What It May Mean</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            ['One isolated leak or damaged area', 'A targeted repair may still be enough if the rest of the roof remains serviceable.'],
            ['Leaks keep appearing in different areas', 'Multiple problems may point to broader deterioration rather than one isolated failure.'],
            ['You have repaired the roof several times', 'It may be worth comparing the value of another repair with the condition of the roof as a whole.'],
            ['Roofing material is deteriorating across several areas', 'Widespread material wear can make continued spot repairs less practical.'],
            ['There are concerns beneath the roofing material', 'Decking or other underlying conditions may affect whether localized repair remains appropriate.'],
            ['The roof is older but has no significant problems', 'Age by itself is not a reason to replace a roof that remains serviceable.'],
          ].map(([seeing, meaning], i) => (
            <tr class:list={['border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-slate-800 last:border-b-0', i % 2 === 1 ? 'bg-gray-50/60 dark:bg-slate-800/30' : '']}>
              <td class="px-5 py-4 text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-heading align-top">{seeing}</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-4 text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted align-top">{meaning}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted italic text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      The goal is not to find a reason to sell you a new roof. It is to determine whether your existing roof can still do its job.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 text-center">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Find Out What Condition Your Roof Is In</a>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <SectionBg variant="grey" />
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Oahu conditions — white -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="text-[26px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading mb-6">
        What Makes an Aging Roof Different on Oahu?
      </h2>
      <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-5">
        <p>Roofs on Oahu are exposed to conditions that can affect materials differently depending on the property, roof type, and location.</p>
        <p>Regular sun and UV exposure can weather exterior roofing materials over time. Wind-driven rain can expose weaknesses around roofing details. Coastal properties may also experience more exposure to salt air, particularly around metal components.</p>
        <p>That does not mean every Oahu roof deteriorates at the same rate. A roof in one neighborhood may age differently from a similar roof somewhere else on the island. Installation history, material, previous repairs, drainage, exposure, and maintenance can all affect its condition.</p>
        <p>That is why R&C does not recommend deciding whether a roof is "too old" based on a generic lifespan number alone.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <SectionBg variant="white" />
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Repair, Replace, or Monitor — grey -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <Headline title="Repair, Replace, or Keep Monitoring?" classes={{ container: 'mb-4 md:mb-6' }} />
    <p class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8 md:mb-10">
      This is the main decision. A roof inspection should help determine which path makes the most sense based on the condition that actually exists.
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 shadow-card">
      <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse bg-white dark:bg-slate-900">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-accent/20 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700">
            <th class="px-5 py-4 text-[13px] md:text-[14px] font-semibold font-heading text-heading uppercase tracking-wide w-1/2">Roof Condition</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-4 text-[13px] md:text-[14px] font-semibold font-heading text-heading uppercase tracking-wide w-1/2">What May Make Sense</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            ['One localized problem and the surrounding roof remains serviceable', 'Repair the affected area.'],
            ['Minor aging is present but the roof is still performing', 'Monitor the condition and address problems as they develop.'],
            ['Repairs are becoming frequent in different parts of the roof', 'Evaluate replacement against the cost and practicality of continuing isolated repairs.'],
            ['Deterioration affects large portions of the roofing system', 'Replacement may make more sense than continuing to chase individual failures.'],
            ['Underlying roofing components show broader problems', 'The replacement discussion should include what needs to be addressed beneath the exterior material.'],
            ['A recent storm caused new damage to an older roof', 'Separate the storm-related condition from longer-term deterioration before deciding what work is appropriate.'],
          ].map(([condition, action], i) => (
            <tr class:list={['border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-slate-800 last:border-b-0', i % 2 === 1 ? 'bg-gray-50/60 dark:bg-slate-800/30' : '']}>
              <td class="px-5 py-4 text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-heading align-top">{condition}</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-4 text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted align-top">{action}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      R&C does not assume that an older roof needs replacement.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      But there is also a point where continuing to repair separate failures can stop being the practical long-term choice.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4 mt-8">
      <a href="/services/roof-repair" class="btn-primary">Explore Roof Repair</a>
      <a href="/services/roof-replacement-and-new-installation" class="btn btn-secondary">Explore Roof Replacement</a>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <SectionBg variant="grey" />
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- If replacement is the answer — white -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-16">
      <div class="lg:basis-1/2">
        <h2 class="text-[26px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading mb-6">
          If Replacement Is the Better Option, What Comes Next?
        </h2>
        <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-4">
          <p>Once the roof condition points toward replacement, the conversation changes from "Do I need a new roof?" to "What should I replace it with?"</p>
          <p>The right roofing material depends on the property, roof design, budget, appearance preferences, and how the building is used.</p>
          <p>Rather than choosing a material based only on what was installed before, compare the options that make sense for the property now.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8">
          <a href="/services/roof-replacement-and-new-installation" class="btn-primary">Explore Roof Replacement &amp; Installation</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:basis-1/2">
        <p class="text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-semibold text-heading mb-4 uppercase tracking-wide">R&C works with several roofing material categories:</p>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { title: 'Metal Roofing', href: '/services/roofing-materials/metal-roofing' },
            { title: 'Asphalt Shingle Roofing', href: '/services/roofing-materials/asphalt-shingle-roofing' },
            { title: 'Stone-Coated Steel Roofing', href: '/services/roofing-materials/stone-coated-steel-roofing' },
            { title: 'Clay and Concrete Tile Roofing', href: '/services/roofing-materials/tile-roofing-clay-and-concrete' },
          ].map(({ title, href }) => (
            <a href={href} class="flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg border border-white/16 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-card p-4 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow intersect-once intersect-quarter motion-safe:md:opacity-0 motion-safe:md:intersect:animate-fade">
              <span class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%]">{title}</span>
              <span class="text-primary font-medium text-[14px]">View →</span>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="mt-4">
          <a href="/services/roofing-materials" class="text-primary font-medium text-[14px] md:text-[15px] hover:underline">Compare All Roofing Materials →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <SectionBg variant="white" />
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Storm + older roof — grey -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="text-[26px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading mb-6">
        What If a Storm Made You Start Questioning an Older Roof?
      </h2>
      <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-5">
        <p>A storm can expose a problem on a roof that was already showing age. That does not mean every condition found afterward was caused by the storm.</p>
        <p>R&C can evaluate the physical roofing condition and help distinguish between localized storm-related damage and broader deterioration where possible.</p>
        <p>If an insurance claim becomes involved, R&C remains on the contractor side. We can inspect and document roofing conditions and provide information about proposed roofing work. Your insurance carrier determines coverage and payment.</p>
        <p class="italic text-[14px] md:text-[15px]">R&C Roofing Contractors is not a public adjuster and does not negotiate insurance settlements, interpret policy coverage, represent policyholders in claim disputes, or guarantee claim outcomes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-8">
        <a href="/storm-damage-on-my-roof" class="btn-primary">Storm Damage on My Roof</a>
        <a href="/roof-inspections/storm-and-wind-damage-inspection" class="btn btn-secondary">Storm &amp; Wind Damage Roof Inspection</a>
        <a href="/insurance-claim-help" class="text-primary font-medium text-[14px] md:text-[15px] hover:underline self-center">Insurance Claim Help →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <SectionBg variant="grey" />
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Related Problems — white -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <Headline title="Does Another Roofing Problem Better Match Your Situation?" classes={{ container: 'mb-4 md:mb-6' }} />
    <p class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8 md:mb-10">
      If one of these situations is closer to what brought you here, continue with the page that matches the problem.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5">
      {[
        {
          title: 'My Roof Is Leaking',
          description: 'Water is coming into the house now.',
          href: '/my-roof-is-leaking',
        },
        {
          title: 'Storm Damage on My Roof',
          description: 'The roof changed after strong wind or severe weather.',
          href: '/storm-damage-on-my-roof',
        },
        {
          title: 'My Insurance Claim Was Denied',
          description: 'Your insurance claim was denied.',
          href: '/my-insurance-claim-was-denied',
        },
        {
          title: 'Buying or Selling a Home',
          description: 'You are trying to understand the roof before buying or selling a property.',
          href: '/buying-or-selling-a-home',
        },
      ].map(({ title, description, href }) => (
        <a href={href} class="rounded-lg border border-white/16 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-card p-5 md:p-6 flex flex-col hover:shadow-md transition-shadow intersect-once intersect-quarter motion-safe:md:opacity-0 motion-safe:md:intersect:animate-fade">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] md:text-[20px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-2">{title}</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted flex-1">{description}</p>
          <span class="mt-3 text-primary font-medium text-[14px]">Continue here →</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <SectionBg variant="white" />
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- FAQs — grey -->
  <FAQs
    title="Frequently Asked Questions About Aging Roofs"
    items={[
      {
        title: 'How do I know when my roof needs to be replaced?',
        description: 'There is no single sign that applies to every roof. Repeated leaks, widespread material deterioration, recurring repairs, and problems affecting multiple roof areas can all be reasons to consider replacement. The overall roof condition matters more than one symptom by itself.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Is my roof too old to repair?',
        description: 'Not necessarily. An older roof may still be repairable when the problem is localized and the surrounding roofing system remains serviceable.',
      },
      {
        title: 'How old should a roof be before it is replaced?',
        description: 'There is no single useful age for every roof. Expected service life depends on the roofing material, product, installation, exposure, maintenance, and actual condition. R&C evaluates the roof itself rather than recommending replacement solely because it has reached a particular age.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Is it worth repairing an old roof?',
        description: 'Sometimes. If the problem is isolated and the rest of the roof remains serviceable, another repair may be reasonable. If different areas continue to fail, it may be worth comparing continued repair with replacement.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Does a leaking older roof automatically need replacement?',
        description: 'No. One leak may come from a localized condition that can be repaired. Multiple leaks or widespread deterioration may point toward a broader roofing issue.',
      },
      {
        title: 'How much does a roof replacement cost on Oahu?',
        description: 'Replacement cost depends on the size and configuration of the roof, material selected, accessibility, existing roof condition, and the scope of work required. R&C can provide project-specific pricing after evaluating the property.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Can I choose a different roofing material when I replace my roof?',
        description: 'Depending on the property and roofing system, another material may be worth considering. Visit our Roofing Materials page to compare the roofing options R&C currently offers.',
      },
    ]}
  >
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <SectionBg variant="grey" />
    </Fragment>
  </FAQs>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <CTABanner
    title="Not Sure Whether to Repair or Replace?"
    subtitle="You do not need to make that decision based only on the age of the roof.<br /><br />Start with its actual condition. R&amp;C can evaluate what is failing, what is still serviceable, and whether another repair or a broader roof replacement makes more sense."
    ctaText="Have R&C Evaluate Your Roof"
  />

</Layout>
